// GDTF authored area-damage FIELD type — "incendiary fire" / burning ground.
// AUTHORED CONTENT (a field-type catalog entry), loaded as a loose `.ron` through
// the RonAsset<FieldDef> loader, keyed by its filename stem `incendiary_fire`.
//
// A temporary hazard: a patch of burning ground (a spilled promethium fire) that sears whoever
// stands on it for a couple of turns, then burns out. A FLAT per-turn HP drain gated only by
// whole-source immunity.
//
// CATALOG PROPOSAL (REVIEW-FLAG — defensible interim defaults):
//   - damage_type Plasma (wheel node 4 — superheated).
//   - immune { Hazard } — Hazard is the Plasma-mirror armor node (a heat-sealed hazmat suit).
//   - Turns(2) — burns out after two turns.
// Magnitudes ARBITRARY interim values; never pinned by a test.
(
    damage:             5,             // FieldDamage — flat HP drained per turn
    damage_type:        Plasma,        // wheel-node flavour (presentation only)
    immune_armor_types: [Hazard],      // whole-source immunity: a Hazard suit seals against the heat
    duration:           Turns(2),      // burns out after 2 turns
)
